      "synthesis": {
        "main_text_has_explicit_synthesis": true,
        "si_used": false,
        "procedure": "General cluster synthesis: Hhpb and neodymium trichloride were combined in a 2:1 molar ratio in a round-bottomed flask, dissolved in methanol, and treated by slow dropwise addition of 4 equivalents of triethylamine. After 24 h the solvent was removed and the residue was stirred in toluene (2 mL) for 1 h, filtered, and left to evaporate. Pale yellow crystals of 1 were obtained (yield 24%). Single crystals suitable for X-ray diffraction were grown by slow diffusion of diethyl ether into a wet DMF solution of 1 over four weeks.",
